//   EWCore Docs        on-chart help and reference panel for EWCore; displays
//                      reference text only and calculates nothing
// EWCoreLib is required for EWCore to work. TradingView loads it automatically
// when EWCore is added to a chart — no separate installation or setup is needed.
// EWCore Docs is optional and is only useful alongside EWCore.
//
// DISCLAIMER
// Technical analysis tooling — not financial advice, not a buy/sell signal
// generator, and not a tested trading strategy.
//
// Elliott Wave analysis is a theory about recurring patterns in market behaviour,
// not a physical law. The "hard rules" enforced here are rules of the counting
// METHOD; they are not a claim that price is obliged to follow them. Documented
// exceptions exist within the theory itself, and experienced analysts routinely
// reach different, equally rule-consistent counts on the same chart. A count that
// satisfies every rule checked is one internally consistent reading among several
// that may be possible — never a guarantee of future price behaviour. Every
// trading decision, and its outcome, remains the user's own.
//
// Reliable counting starts at M15. M1 and M5 are not, or only conditionally,
